        "original_id": "2ae940d2-4adc-5156-b390-1e01097b12fa",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Albert Gallatin, Marmaduke Williams\n- Works: The Probability Broach\n- Places: Gallatin National Forest, North American continent\n- Organizations: Democratic-Republican Party, North American Confederacy\n- Concepts: Gallatin Universe, alternate history, libertarian society\n\nFacts:\n- Albert Gallatin was born on January 29, 1761, and died on August 12, 1849.\n- Albert Gallatin was a Swiss-American politician, diplomat, ethnologist, and linguist.\n- Albert Gallatin was an important leader of the Democratic-Republican Party and served in federal elective and appointed positions across four decades.\n- Marmaduke Williams was born on April 6, 1774, and died on October 29, 1850.\n- Marmaduke Williams was a Democratic-Republican U.S. Congressman from North Carolina from 1803 to 1809.\n- Gallatin National Forest is named after Albert Gallatin, who was U.S. Secretary of the Treasury and a scholar of Native American languages and cultures.\n- The Probability Broach is set in an alternate-history setting called the Gallatin Universe.\n- In The Probability Broach, the Gallatin Universe depicts a libertarian society on the North American continent called the North American Confederacy, or NAC.",
